  "aboutTitle": "About Auto Crónica",
  "aboutFounderPhoto": "Portrait of Daniel Fonseca da Silva",
  "aboutLead": "My name's Daniel Fonseca da Silva. I'm a software engineer based in Portugal nearly nine years spent building reliable systems, from the cloud to the products people use every day and I'm also a car enthusiast. Auto Crónica came out of where those two things meet.",
  "aboutLinkedinLabel": "View LinkedIn profile",
  "aboutProblemTitle": "The problem",
  "aboutProblemBody": "Anywhere in Europe, buying a car new or used often means going in blind. Every vehicle has faults that surface sooner or later: a part that always fails in the same place, an engine with a known weakness, a gearbox that gives trouble past a certain mileage. That information exists, but it's scattered across forums, groups and loose conversations and it's hard to know what to trust.",
  "aboutSolutionTitle": "The solution",
  "aboutSolutionBody": "Auto Crónica is a catalogue of chronic faults organised by make and model, built to grow over time. When there isn't enough data yet on a vehicle, AI helps suggest the most likely issues; and a community of owners comments, corrects and votes on reports, so the information keeps getting more reliable.",
  "aboutCommunityTitle": "For anyone who loves cars",
  "aboutCommunityBody": "This project is for anyone who loves practical city cars, quiet electrics, characterful classics or sporty machines and wants to decide with more information and fewer surprises.",
